##### README file - Steps to run simulation for SM (Sundance Mesa) System-Example-Design PCIe Rootport #####

      1. Git repo:  To clone a fresh repository (this step need to do once for new repo)
      % git clone https://github.com/altera-fpga/agilex5-ed-pcie-rp.git

      2. ITF resources:  Get ITF resources for Makefile/ITF/SpetC (do once for new window)
      %arc shell vcs-vcsmx-lic,acdskit/<ver>,devacds/<ver>,testutils/<ver>,regutils/<ver>,itf/<ver>,ostype/suse15,synopsys_vip_common/<vip_Q-2020.03A>,p4/psgeng,perl/<ver>
      Ex: arc shell vcs-vcsmx-lic,acds/26.3,devacds/23.4,testutils/23.4/79,regutils/23.4,itf/23.4,ostype/suse15,synopsys_vip_common/vip_W-2025.03C,p4/psgeng,perl/5.8.8
    #synopsys/vip_common/vip_W-2025.03C

      3. Makefile :  Get Makefile env and set up
      %setenv REG_LOCAL_ROOT_DIR_PATH <working directory>
      EX: %setenv REG_LOCAL_ROOT_DIR_PATH /nfs/site/disks/swuser_work_susanttr/git_altr1/sm_pcie_rp/applications.fpga.system-example-designs.agilex5-ed-pcie-rp/src/hw/a5e065bb32aes1_pdk/verification/

          bash use export:
          %export REG_LOCAL_ROOT_DIR_PATH=/nfs/site/disks/swuser_work_drajarat/2351_ITF/src/hw/verification

      %cd $REG_LOCAL_ROOT_DIR_PATH/../env/sm_4x4
      (Note: need to use bash mode (/usr/intel/bin/bash) while sourcing the env.sh and setup.sh)
      %source env.sh
      %source setup.sh
  
      4. Run regression with Makefile/ITF/Spetc Manually or cronjob:
         4a. Run regression manually with Makefile/ITF/SpetC. (Note: Update the regr_launch.sh to your working directory)
             %cd  $REG_LOCAL_ROOT_DIR_PATH/scripts/itf
             Manually follow step by step in regr_launch.sh

         4b. Run regression through cronjob
         MAILTO="<email_addr>"
         <time> <Date> arc submit <resource> --<commnad>

         Example: sync with latest, launch SM PCIe RP every Monday at 5:30am, email launch information to <owner> 
         --------
	    MAILTO="susan.tran@altera.com"
            20 5 * * 1 cd /nfs/site/disks/swuser_work_susanttr/git_altr1/sm_pcie_rp/applications.fpga.system-example-designs.agilex5-ed-pcie-rp/src/hw/a5e065bb32aes1_pdk; /usr/intel/bin/git pull

	    30 5 * * 1 /p/psg/ctools/arc/2019.1/bin/arc submit vcs-vcsmx-lic,acdskit/25.1,devacds/23.4,testutils/23.4/79,regutils/23.4,itf/23.4,ostype/suse15,synopsys_vip_common/vip_Q-2020.03A,p4/psgeng,perl/5.8.8,python/3.7.7/1,gcc/12.2.0/3,cmake/3.11.4,vcs/V-2023.12-SP2-1  -- /nfs/site/disks/swuser_work_susanttr/git_altr1/sm_pcie_rp/applications.fpga.system-example-designs.agilex5-ed-pcie-rp/src/hw/a5e065bb32aes1_pdk/verification/scripts/itf/regr_launch.sh

      
      //====================================================================
      FYI, here are the details of Makefile/ITF/Spetc

      A. The following ITF files are needed under .../verification/scripts/itf in order to run regression in ITF/Spetc
            sanity_regr
            SetEnv.pm
            RegressionList.pm
            itf_common.pm
            prev //directory
            reg_test.pl
            reg_info
            flow.txt
            itf_regtest_local.pl
            regr_launch.sh


      B. Makefile/ITF/Spetc flow:
         MK: Makefile
         ITF: reg_test/reg_exe
                                                                             MK: run sim: gmake -f Makefile.mk run TESTNAME=<test>
      MK:env,setup                MK: qsys              MK: build           /
      GET RESOURCES --------------GEN RTL files---------BUILD SIMV ------- RUN SIM/REGR
      ITF resources                                                         \
                                                                             ITF: regr_launch.sh
      %more regr_launch.sh
        #1. Git pull to get the latest files from git repo (TBA)
	#2 source env.sh and setup.sh for Makefile qsys/rtl and build
        /usr/intel/bin/bash
	export REG_LOCAL_ROOT_DIR_PATH=/nfs/site/disks/swuser_work_susanttr/git_altr1/sm_pcie_rp/applications.fpga.system-example-designs.agilex5-ed-pcie-rp/src/hw/a5e065bb32aes1_pdk/verification
	source $REG_LOCAL_ROOT_DIR_PATH/../env/sm_4x4/env.sh
	/usr/intel/bin/bash 
	source $REG_LOCAL_ROOT_DIR_PATH/../env/sm_4x4/setup.sh
	cd $REG_LOCAL_ROOT_DIR_PATH/scripts/sm_4x4 && /p/psg/flows/sw/make_altera/4.3/linux64/gmake -f Makefile.mk cmplib && /p/psg/flows/sw/make_altera/4.3/linux64/gmake -f Makefile.mk build REGR=1
	32 Cleanup old files, launch regression through ITF flow and generate Spetc report
	cd $REG_LOCAL_ROOT_DIR_PATH/scripts/itf
	/p/psg/flows/sw/regutils/23.4/5/linux64/bin/reg_reset
	/p/psg/flows/sw/regutils/23.4/5/linux64/bin/reg_exe --local --title="SIM-AGX7-FTILEPTP" --regr_cfg=sanity_regr | tee t.log
	/p/psg/flows/sw/regutils/23.4/5/linux64/bin/reg_exe --farm --title="SIM-AGX7-FTILEPTP" --regr_cfg=sanity_regr | tee t.log


# SM7PLUS PTP — How to run ITF

ITF directory (from clone root):
  <clone>/src/hw/verification/scripts/itf

Do not mix 10G and 25G in one xterm.

<clone> = top of this git clone (the directory that contains src/).

------------------------------------------------
1. Go to ITF directory
------------------------------------------------
cd <clone>/src/hw/verification/scripts/itf

------------------------------------------------
2. Load ARC / ITF resources (once per window)
------------------------------------------------
arc shell vcs-vcsmx-lic,acds/26.3,devacds/23.4,testutils/23.4/79,regutils/23.4,itf/23.4,ostype/suse15,synopsys_vip_common/vip_W-2025.03C,p4/psgeng,perl/5.8.8,python/3.7.7/1,vcsmx/X-2025.06-SP1-1,synopsys_verdi/U-2023.03-SP2-1

If versions change, copy the resource list from the arc submit line in sim_script_part1.sh.

------------------------------------------------
3. Launch farm regression
------------------------------------------------
25G:
  sh sim_script_part1.sh 25g

10G:
  sh sim_script_part1.sh 10g

Wait until all sequence__* tests finish.

Logs:
  SIM_SED_SM7PLUSPTP_PDK_25G_STDOUT.out
  SIM_SED_SM7PLUSPTP_PDK_10G_STDOUT.out

------------------------------------------------
4. HTML / email report
------------------------------------------------
25G:
  python3 sim_part2.py 25g

10G:
  python3 sim_part2.py 10g

Report file:
  sm7plus_simulation_test.html

------------------------------------------------
5. Check results
------------------------------------------------
ls sequence__*.sem.pass
cat SIM_SED_SM7PLUSPTP_PDK_25G_STDOUT.out
cat SIM_SED_SM7PLUSPTP_PDK_10G_STDOUT.out

SPeTC and ARC job links are available in the mail. Click the SPeTC Id and ARC Job Id in the report email.

Pass marker: sequence__<test>.sem.pass

